{"title":"2022 SSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In regular hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> with side length 1, an electron starts at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. When the electron hits an edge, it reflects off of it, with the angle of reflection equal to the angle of incidence. The electron first travels in a straight line to a point on edge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. The electron bounces off of a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> edges before hitting a vertex. The electron stops and its total distance traveled is measured. The shortest possible distance the electron could have traveled can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c707f01031d7f0a1e7ec87f782a715b580482d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d8917ab129f63c7f01f0713d183fa853284125.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(10cm); pair A = (1,0); pair B = (1/2,sqrt(3)/2); pair C = (-1/2,sqrt(3)/2); pair D = (-1,0); pair E = (-1/2,-sqrt(3)/2); pair F = (1/2,-sqrt(3)/2);  pair A_ = (-2,sqrt(3)); pair B_ = (-1,sqrt(3)); pair C_ = (-1/2,sqrt(3)/2); pair D_ = (-1,0); pair E_ = (-2,0); pair F_ = (-5/2,sqrt(3)/2);  pair A__ = (-7/2,sqrt(3)/2); pair B__ = (-4,0); pair C__ = (-7/2,-sqrt(3)/2); pair D__ = (-5/2,-sqrt(3)/2); pair F__ = (-5/2,sqrt(3)/2); pair E__ = (-2,0);  pair A___ = (-7/2,sqrt(3)/2); pair B___ = (-4,sqrt(3)); pair C___ = (-7/2,3*sqrt(3)/2); pair D___ = (-5/2,3*sqrt(3)/2); pair E___ = (-2,sqrt(3)); pair F___ = (-5/2,sqrt(3)/2);  pair A____ = (-7/2,sqrt(3)/2); pair B____ = (-4,sqrt(3)); pair C____ = (-5,sqrt(3)); pair D____ = (-11/2,sqrt(3)/2); pair E____ = (-5,0); pair F____ = (-4,0);  pair A_____ = (-13/2,3*sqrt(3)/2); pair B_____ = (-11/2,3*sqrt(3)/2); pair C_____ = (-5,sqrt(3)); pair D_____ = (-11/2,sqrt(3)/2); pair E_____ = (-13/2,sqrt(3)/2); pair F_____ = (-7,sqrt(3));  draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--cycle); draw(A_--B_--C_--D_--E_--F_--cycle,dashed+blue); draw(A__--B__--C__--D__--E__--F__--cycle,dashed+blue); draw(A___--B___--C___--D___--E___--F___--cycle,dashed+blue); draw(A____--B____--C____--D____--E____--F____--cycle,dashed+blue); draw(A_____--B_____--C_____--D_____--E_____--F_____--cycle,dashed+blue); draw(A--F_____,dashed+red+linewidth(1.2));   dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,dir(0)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,dir(45)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,dir(45)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,dir(225)); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,dir(225)); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,dir(315));  dot(&quot;$A&#39;$&quot;,A_,dir(45),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$B&#39;$&quot;,B_,dir(45),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$E&#39;$&quot;,E_,dir(45),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$F&#39;$&quot;,F_,dir(120),fontsize(8pt));  dot(&quot;$A&#39;&#39;$&quot;,A__,dir(300),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$B&#39;&#39;$&quot;,B__,dir(0),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$C&#39;&#39;$&quot;,C__,dir(45),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$D&#39;&#39;$&quot;,D__,dir(120),fontsize(8pt));  dot(&quot;$B&#39;&#39;&#39;$&quot;,B___,dir(120),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$C&#39;&#39;$&quot;,C___,dir(90),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$D&#39;&#39;&#39;$&quot;,D___,dir(90),fontsize(8pt));  dot(&quot;$C&#39;&#39;&#39;&#39;$&quot;,C____,dir(45),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$D&#39;&#39;&#39;&#39;$&quot;,D____,dir(0),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$E&#39;&#39;&#39;&#39;$&quot;,E____,dir(45),fontsize(8pt));  dot(&quot;$A&#39;&#39;&#39;&#39;&#39;$&quot;,A_____,dir(90),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$B&#39;&#39;&#39;&#39;&#39;$&quot;,B_____,dir(90),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$E&#39;&#39;&#39;&#39;&#39;$&quot;,E_____,dir(45),fontsize(8pt)); dot(&quot;$F&#39;&#39;&#39;&#39;&#39;$&quot;,F_____,2*dir(30),fontsize(8pt)); [/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"232\" /> </center><p> We repeatedly reflect the hexagon to achieve a ring of hexagons. Our answer is the shortest path from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to a vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> on ring such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d857b2c804701b561a5c8c90c400f360d27232c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" /> passes through 5 edges of the ring of hexagons. Shown above is the shortest possible path, which involves passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, which has a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be9a9087afa0bbb75848512c3ebebe7a7b25eb6d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{8^2+\\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{67}\\implies\\boxed{67}.\\]\" width=\"248\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022217\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.017 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 65/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5490/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26213:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022217 and revision id 280173. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}